WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:05.680
Hey YouTubers! It's Charlie. So season 5 episode 1 is getting ready to air tonight. 

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:10.280
So I wanted to do a bonus video for the Sons of the Harpy, one of the organizations inside Meereen.

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:15.140
There's also a lot of news is going around. Some big stuff happened yesterday. So I'll address that at the end of the video too.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:18.900
Careful for spoilers for everything from season 1 to season 4 on the show

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:24.880
The Sons of the Harpy are a counter-insurgent group, put together by the noble houses of Meereen

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:27.100
before Dany moved in; the slaving houses.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:30.700
They're basically 10 big families that all live in like really big pyramids.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:34.320
They controlled the city before Daenerys moved in and abolished slavery.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:38.400
They're pissed. They don't like the idea of democracy, which is basically what Daenerys represents. 

00:00:38.541 --> 00:00:44.101
So what you have going on in Slaver's bay right now is very much like an American Civil War situation

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:48.880
where the states are like 'Hey we still like slavery. We want to keep doing things the way we've done them forever.'

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:50.800
Daenerys is like 'Nope. Not gonna happen'.

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:56.380
Even though she has the Unsullied, the Second Sons, her dragons, and a lot of very grateful freedmen, 

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:58.920
it's still not quite enough to overpower the ruling families.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:04.480
The name the Sons of the Harpy derives from the symbol the harpy of the old Ghiscari Empire

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:09.020
This is where it gets really interesting because a lot of historical events in George R.R. Martins's books

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:11.760
in the Song of Ice and Fire repeat themselves 

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:14.240
'This has all happened before. This will all happen again'

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:15.540
It's a very Battlestar type of idea. 

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:20.375
If you look at this image in the trailer of them pulling the Harpy down off the top of the pyramid,

00:01:20.375 --> 00:01:23.133
It's a methaphor for the fall of the Ghiscari Empire.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:26.080
The Valyrians crushed them using their dragons. 

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:30.660
So Daenerys, Valyrian descendent, has come into Meereen and is tearing down slavery 

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:35.560
So you can think of this like a mini-version of the Valyrian's war against the Ghiscari 

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:41.634
To be fair though, the Ghiscari weren't like crazy awful people and they didn't even create the name Slaver's Bay.

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:45.214
Although they did originate all the major cities of Slaver's Bay.

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:48.220
Just to refresh your memory that's Astapor, 

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:52.520
Yunkai (that's where the wise masters are - the last big group of people she defeated before she came to Meereen), 

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:55.940
and then Meereen, the largest city in Slaver's Bay.

00:01:56.420 --> 00:02:00.460
The reason it's called Slaver's Bay, the reason why slavery became such a problem,

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:04.174
is because that rose up in the ashes of the Ghiscari Empire.

00:02:04.174 --> 00:02:08.154
Like after the Valyrians crushed them, it made it impossible for them to grow new crops.

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:11.700
People in the area turned to slavery to survive. 

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:16.460
So you could look at slavery, the Sons of the Harpy, and the problem that Daenerys has trying to abolish it

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:18.300
as being caused by the Valyrians.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:24.020
Sometimes the best problems are the you create for yourself and that's true of all characters on Game of Thrones.

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:29.300
Jaime Lannister caused so many problems, so many consequences that he didn't think about ahead of time.

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:33.240
Cersei Lannister same thing. So Daenerys has a civil war on her hands.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:36.880
The Sons of the Harpy rising up, trying to push her out of Meereen.

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:40.440
The person giving them orders in the books is called The Harpy.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.680
I don't know if they're gonna have that person on the show or not. 

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:48.560
So far it's a mystery person but the most likely candidate in the books is someone that the show has not introduced yet.

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:53.380
It's not a character on the show. What I think is going to end up happening on the show is that it'll be Hizdahr.

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:57.900
During season 4, he was introduced as the envoy of the slaving families. 

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:03.255
So he is like the representative of the old guard in Meereen, the people that still want to slave.

00:03:03.255 --> 00:03:07.335
He seems really nice but we'll see where that goes. He's kind of like a Varys-type person.

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:09.200
He keeps his cards pretty close to the vest. 

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:13.340
It should go without saying that the show is going to change a lot of things from the books.

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:17.740
But as I go along with my episode videos, I'll try to explain what they did and why they did it.

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:20.940
What about solutions though? How is Daenerys gonna solve this problem?

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:26.040
Well if she acted like the old Valyrians she would just used her dragons to roast them alive.

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:30.400
The problem is, is that her dragons are chained up and Drogon is roaming gods know where.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:35.700
She also wants to think of herself as a liberator; a benevolent mother, Meesa. That's what that term means.

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:40.560
Using dragons to roast her opponents alive is something that her father would do, The Mad King.

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:42.180
She doesn't want to be like her dad.

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:48.680
So it's going to be really interesting to see her try to balance her true nature as a Targaryen, mother of dragons

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:51.360
and her desire to be the mother of these new people.

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:57.780
It's like when your child is first growing up, you know, a lot of people say you can't be either best friend AND their parent at the same time.

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.100
It's only much, much later in life that that can happen.

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:03.760
Right now all these people on Meereen are like little children trying to learn a new way.

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:08.780
So it's either going to be the carrot or the stick. Or like a stick of fire if you want to use the dragon analogy.

00:04:09.098 --> 00:04:16.098
When you think about the whole situation, it's kind of funny because she's really just trying to fix a very small part of the Eastern continent. 

00:04:16.098 --> 00:04:18.258
It seems like it is much bigger than it actually is.

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:24.100
Slavery is a big problem. Slaver's Bay is just like the central location for slavery in the Eastern continent. 

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:28.320
It's not like she's trying to subdue the entire Eastern continent. It's massive.

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:34.540
Just look at the Dorthraki Sea here. Then you have like the Iron Bank, all the money up in Braavos. That's a whole other story.

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:40.080
But if she can subdue and unite Slaver's Bay, she will have an army big enough to take Westeros.

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:44.960
She doesn't need to conquer the entire Eastern continent. She just needs to win popular opinion.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:51.260
So I guess when you think about it though, the Sons of the Harpy are really just like co-opting the name of an empire that fell.

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:57.880
That they bare very little resemblance to. The Ghirscari weren't even that bad. It was just what things turned into after the empire fell.

00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:05.860
We will probably get like a much better look around the streets of Meereen. There are actually statues of harpies all over the place.

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:09.600
That's Ghiscari architecture. There are a couple of places that we will be seeing in Meereen that we haven't seen before.

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:14.060
Including the fighting pits. Most notably Daznak's Pit. That's where they are right here in this scene.

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:17.420
As you can see the Harpies want Daenerys's head on a pike. 

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:19.920
The fighting pits are self-explanatory though

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:26.100
There are good examples of an entertainment devices used by the slaving families historically to keep the citizens happy.

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:30.920
It would be like erecting a giant movie theater in the middle of like a low-income housing district. 

00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:36.960
It'd be like 'Yea we understand you don't have any money. We know things are bad but here have some entertainment, free entertainment'.

00:05:37.214 --> 00:05:40.834
In Ancient Rome, the colosseum ended up being used the exact same way.

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:46.280
People could come see fights and get free food. Sometimes the Caesars would give away free bread. 

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:50.600
So like peasants could come and get free bread and watch people bleed all over the place.

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:54.696
Daenerys, as you can imagine, not a huge fan of this. So we'll see what's going to win out.

00:05:54.838 --> 00:06:00.818
Daenerys, you know, trying to be this rational mother person or classic Targaryen mother of dragons.

00:06:00.818 --> 00:06:03.138
One of the things I always really love about this show is that

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:09.880
even if you spend a lot of time in the same cities season to season they always find new place to film; new locations.

00:06:09.887 --> 00:06:13.827
